.TH "EPX\-DELIVERY\-TIMES" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-delivery\-times \- read and change delivery times and their time slots; read the delivery windows of a cart
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times [flags]
epx delivery\-times [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes delivery times, the days on which a site delivers to a zone, and their time slots; reads the delivery windows open to a cart, checks and counts the orders of a delivery window and names its delivery cycle.
.PP
Its reads require different OAuth scopes; the help of each names them. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx delivery\-times bulk\-create"
Create delivery times in bulk.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times bulk\-create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the delivery times in \fB\-\-file\fR, a JSON array of delivery times, each as create takes it.
.PP
Emporix takes up to 50 items in one request (epx refuses more), carries out each on its own and answers with the result of each: when one failed, epx prints the response, lists the items that failed on standard error (one that failed with 500, 502, 503 or 504 may have been carried out all the same) and exits with the code that their failures share (for example 5 for a 409 Conflict, 4 for a 404), else 1.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-overlap <string>\fR
Whether Emporix refuses slots of one shipping method whose time ranges overlap (it does unless given false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx delivery\-times create"
Create a delivery time.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a delivery time from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its siteCode and zoneId (or isForAllZones, for a day without delivery on every zone of the site), its day (a weekday, singleDate or datePeriod), isDeliveryDay, timeZoneId and deliveryDayShift, the slots of a delivery day and optionally the delivery time\(aqs id and name, as \fBepx delivery\-times get ID \-o json\fR prints one; a slot with a cutOffDayShift needs a delivery time without deliveryDayShift. Emporix answers with its id, and refuses a delivery time that overlaps another of its zone, or is not valid otherwise, with 400 Bad Request (exit 1).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-overlap <string>\fR
Whether Emporix refuses slots of one shipping method whose time ranges overlap (it does unless given false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx delivery\-times delete"
Delete a delivery time.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the delivery time ID with its time slots. Emporix answers an unknown ID as one that it deleted (204 No Content).
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx delivery\-times generate\-cycle"
Name the delivery cycle of a delivery window.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times generate\-cycle [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Prints the name of the delivery cycle of a delivery window, as Emporix names it in the delivery windows of a cart and in orders (deliveryCycle in \fBepx delivery\-times windows CART_ID \-o json\fR): the delivery date, the hour (UTC) of the slot\(aqs cut\-off time and the deliveryCycleName of its cutOffTime, such as 2026\-06\-20\-6morning. The delivery window is the delivery time \fB\-\-delivery\-time\fR on \fB\-\-date\fR, an ISO 8601 date and time such as 2026\-11\-02T12:00:00.000Z, in its \fB\-\-slot\fR: \fBepx delivery\-times list\fR and \fBepx delivery\-times slots list\fR show their IDs. Emporix answers an unknown delivery time with 403 Forbidden (exit 3), not as not found.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among CYCLE.
.TP
\fB\-\-date <DATE>\fR
The delivery DATE and time, ISO 8601 (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-delivery\-time <ID>\fR
The delivery time\(aqs ID (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot <ID>\fR
The ID of the delivery time\(aqs slot (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.SS "epx delivery\-times get"
Show one delivery time.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads delivery times, the days on which a site delivers to a zone. ZONE is a zone id (\fBepx shipping zones list \-\-site S\fR), or \fB"all zones"\fR for a day without delivery on every zone; DAY is a weekday, a date or a date period (from/to); DELIVERS is false for a day without delivery; DAY SHIFT is how many days the delivery follows an order placed before the cut\-off, when the delivery time sets it (a weekday\(aqs slots may set their own); SLOTS counts the time slots, which \fBepx delivery\-times slots list DELIVERY_TIME_ID\fR lists.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, SITE, ZONE, DAY, DELIVERS, TIME ZONE, DAY SHIFT, SLOTS.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx delivery\-times increment\-counter"
Count one more order in a delivery window.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times increment\-counter [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Counts one more order in a delivery window that has capacity left. The delivery window is the delivery time \fB\-\-delivery\-time\fR on \fB\-\-date\fR, an ISO 8601 date and time such as 2026\-11\-02T12:00:00.000Z, in its \fB\-\-slot\fR: \fBepx delivery\-times list\fR and \fBepx delivery\-times slots list\fR show their IDs. The Checkout Service counts each order that it places with a delivery window; only a checkout of your own needs this. Emporix answers true once it counted the order, and a window that is full or not offered that day, or a date in the past or in another format, with 400 Bad Request (exit 1). The body may also come whole from \fB\-\-file\fR.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-date <DATE>\fR
The delivery DATE and time, ISO 8601 (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-delivery\-time <ID>\fR
The delivery time\(aqs ID (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte instead of the one that epx makes (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot <ID>\fR
The ID of the delivery time\(aqs slot (required without \fB\-\-file\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
