.SS "epx delivery\-times slots"
Read and change the time slots of a delivery time.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times slots [flags]
epx delivery\-times slots [command]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads and changes the time slots of a delivery time.
.PP
Its reads require the shipping.shipping_read scope. Its writes require the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.SS "epx delivery\-times slots create"
Create a time slot of a delivery time.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times slots create DELIVERY_TIME_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a time slot of a delivery day from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR: its shippingMethod (a method of the delivery time\(aqs zone), deliveryTimeRange (timeFrom and timeTo, local times such as 08:00), cutOffTime (its time, an ISO 8601 timestamp whose time of day counts, and for a weekday its cutOffDayShift, which the delivery time must not combine with a deliveryDayShift), capacity (the orders it takes) and optionally its id, as \fBepx delivery\-times slots get DELIVERY_TIME_ID ID \-o json\fR prints one. Emporix answers with its id, and a slot id that exists already with 400 Bad Request (exit 1), not as a conflict. DELIVERY_TIME_ID is the ID that \fBepx delivery\-times list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the shipping.shipping_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-validate\-overlap <string>\fR
Whether Emporix refuses slots of one shipping method whose time ranges overlap (it does unless given false): true or false.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
