.nf
epx delivery\-times validate [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Checks whether a delivery window can take an order. The delivery window is the delivery time \fB\-\-delivery\-time\fR on \fB\-\-date\fR, an ISO 8601 date and time such as 2026\-11\-02T12:00:00.000Z, in its \fB\-\-slot\fR: \fBepx delivery\-times list\fR and \fBepx delivery\-times slots list\fR show their IDs. VALID is true when it can; Emporix answers a date in the past or in another format, or a window that is full or not offered that day, with 400 Bad Request (exit 1), and an unknown delivery time as not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among VALID.
.TP
\fB\-\-date <DATE>\fR
The delivery DATE and time, ISO 8601 (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-delivery\-time <ID>\fR
The delivery time\(aqs ID (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-slot <ID>\fR
The ID of the delivery time\(aqs slot (required without \fB\-\-body\fR).
.SS "epx delivery\-times windows"
List the delivery windows open to a cart.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx delivery\-times windows CART_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the delivery windows in which a cart can be delivered to the country and postal code set on the cart. DATE is the delivery day, FROM and TO the delivery time range on it, METHOD the shipping method, ZONE the shipping zone, CUT\-OFF the latest time to order for the window, SLOT the time slot of its delivery time, which \fBepx delivery\-times slots list DELIVERY_TIME_ID\fR lists, and ID the id of that delivery time (\fBepx delivery\-times get ID\fR); the delivery cycle is only in \fB\-o json\fR. For another postal code than the cart\(aqs, run \fBepx api get /shipping/{tenant}/actualDeliveryWindows/CART_ID \-p postalCode=CODE\fR. CART_ID is the id of a cart; an unknown one is not found (exit 4).
.PP
No OAuth scope is needed.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among DATE, FROM, TO, METHOD, ZONE, CUT\-OFF, SLOT, ID.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
